-- Assertions written by hand from the first line of the entry in the text.
-- "Act—see the following sections:" is a signpost.
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: Act`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `a signpost definition`
-- "ACT means the Australian Capital Territory."
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: ACT`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means`
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: ACT`'s `meaning as printed` EQUALS "ACT means the Australian Capital Territory."
-- "business day means a day that is not—" followed by paragraphs.
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: business day`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means`
-- "calendar year means a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January."
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: calendar year`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means`
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: calendar year`'s `meaning as printed` EQUALS "calendar year means a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January."
-- "document means any record of information, and includes—"
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: document`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means and includes`
-- "function includes authority, duty and power."
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: function`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `includes`
-- "instrument—see section 14." and "may—see section 146."
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: instrument`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `a signpost definition`
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: may`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `a signpost definition`
-- "month means a period beginning at the start of any day of one of the calendar months and ending—"
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: month`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means`
-- "public holiday means a day that is a public holiday in the ACT under the Holidays Act 1958, section 3."
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: public holiday`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means`
-- "working day means a day that is not—" followed by paragraphs.
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: working day`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `means`
-- "writing includes any way of representing or reproducing words in visible form."
#ASSERT `dictionary pt 1: writing`'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `includes`
-- The lookup by term finds an entry by the term as the dictionary prints it.
#ASSERT `dictionary: the in-scope entry for the term` "month" EQUALS JUST `dictionary pt 1: month`

-- An entry that no in-scope provision uses and that is not about time, commencement, laws, instruments or the Territory is not in the module.
#ASSERT `dictionary: the in-scope entry for the term` "dentist" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `dictionary: the in-scope entry for the term` "no such term" EQUALS NOTHING
